\[x^2 + 4x^4 + 4fx^2 + f^2 = 4x^4 + 4dx^2 + d^2.\]Matching coefficients, we get
\begin{align*}
1 + 4f &= 4d, \\
f^2 &= d^2.
\end{align*}From the first equation, $d - f = \frac{1}{4}.$  Since $f^2 = d^2,$ $f = d$ or $f = -d.$  We cannot have $f = d,$ so $f = -d.$  Then $2d = \frac{1}{4},$ so $d = \frac{1}{8}.$

